{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And to his father he sent like this.</b> Like the gift to Benjamin. And along with this he sent ten donkeys and ten she-donkeys, for in the plural the vav at the end is joined [to the word], as in יִשָּׂשכָר זְבוּלוּן וּבִנְיָמִין (Exodus 1:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "Sforno explains the grammatical form עֲשָׂרָה (rather than עֲשֶׂרֶת), reading the final vav as a plural-conjoining particle based on the forms in Exodus 1:2."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:47.764805778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}